{"type":"message","id":"06e18626","parentId":"e50d2dd3","timestamp":"2026-06-02T02:16:05.110Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! `/send` as a GET returns \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" with 200. And `/api/send` also works with GET. But POST returns 500. Let me try the POST with the right content type and a simpler body format, or maybe the `/send` is a GET endpoint and messages are sent differently.\n\nActually, wait - looking at the task description again: \"用POST /send发消息到对应thread\". The platform clearly uses POST for sending. Let me try different content types or parameter formats.\n\nLet me also try to check if maybe the POST needs a different path structure like `/api/v1/send` or the body should be form-encoded instead of JSON.\n\n\nThe API documentation lists `GET /history?threadId=xxx&limit=5` as the history endpoint and `POST /send` for sending messages, but the fact that GET on `/send` works suggests it might be handling both methods. Since JSON POST is returning 500, I should test with `application/x-www-form-urlencoded` encoding instead.","thinkingSignature":"c7d6e50cf139c9dc4687fb9873c8fe5757c1b51f2e1d8f0fa411a3ff7a6b37b2"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_o9x3u8pmltua_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: ***\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded\" \\\n  -d \"threadId=arbitration&content=Heartbeat+02:15+UTC\" -w \"\\nHTTP_CODE:%{http_code}\" 2>&1"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":79,"output":338,"cacheRead":22144,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22561,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780366558416,"responseId":"066d6fdee871cd630e54997c01cecdf5"}}
